  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Circular Textile Trade Mission Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ready Made Garment (RMG) industry, a cornerstone of Bangladesh&apos;s economy, employs over four million people and contributes 10.35% to the gross domestic product (GDP). Despite its economic significance, the sector faces criticism for its substantial environmental footprint, including significant waste generation and resource consumption. Embracing circular practices presents an opportunity to address these challenges, turning waste into a driver of economic growth and environmental responsibility.To reach a circular RMG industry, Bangladesh needs access to new technologies, innovations and knowledge. Organising a trade mission focusing on Bangladesh&apos;s RMG industry (as part of the combi-track Circular Textiles) will offer opportunities to strengthen the relationship between Bangladesh and the Netherlands and enhance private sector and economic cooperation in the circular textile industry in the following sub-sectors:&#x2022;	Recycling of post-production waste;&#x2022;	Traceability;&#x2022;	Clean production (less use of chemicals, water and fossil energy and more use of green energy).</narrative>
  </description>
